{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/790434-vampires-in-the-near-future","id":790434,"title":"Vampires in the near future","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-21T12:50:39-08:00","id":790434,"title":"Vampires in the near future","content":"I am deeply sorry if this has been adressed elsewhere on the forum, but its magnitude can be a bit overwhelming.<br /> <br /> So, in a few weeks I'll be running a Vampire campaign, only in a setting that can be best described as &quot;near future science-fiction&quot;, i.e. the world of today, only tweaked a bit, technology-wise. More cyberpunk-ish, rather than cyberpunk. My problem is that I have no idea how to include the technological advancements (and what would the exactly be, for that matter) in the game without giving them all of the spotlight and not keeping them entirely on the background. In other words, I want to make it a small yet vital part of the campaign and I'd appreciate any practical advice on doing so, especially from people speaking from experience. Here is some additional information to specify the circumstances:<br /> <br /> - The scenery is a 2-milion-and something city in Central Europe, relatively ethnically homogenous, save for a substantial Ukrainian and Vietnamese diasporas.<br /> - The characters aren't exactly decided yet, but they will likely be someone from the outer fringe of society: homeless people, impoverished artists, indebted students etc. They start as mortals and the supernatural should be limited to vampires, maybe with a God-Machine flavor<br /> - Since my intended themes are ever-present paranoia, exploring new, terrifying layers of familiar places/people and facing the unknown, I was thinking about the tech in question being some form of population control and surveillance system(s).<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for every response.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:00:14-08:00","id":790442,"title":"","content":"I believe <b>World of Darkness: Mirrors</b> contains material for cyberpunk-like chronicles. Other than that, I the advice I can give you is to provide NPCs tech-heads who'd have access (or information) regarding the latest pieces of tech. You don't need give 'em a full catalog, just display the neat stuff thru the NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:01:14-08:00","id":790444,"title":"","content":"Have you checked out <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/87936/Mirrors-Bleeding-Edge\" target=\"_blank\">Bleeding Edge</a>? It is the cyberpunk book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:14:17-08:00","id":790448,"title":"","content":"I am familiar with Bleeding Edge, but it proved to be much less informative than I'd hoped. Too watered down for my tastes, not nearly as inspirational than the other books. Plus, it's still cyberpunk, and I need something more like &quot;Minority Report&quot; or Watch_Dogs videogame - a single technological element rather than a whole array of cyberlimbs, implants and AIs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:32:02-08:00","id":790452,"title":"","content":"Significantly expanded surveillance would be Hell for Requiem vampires. A small but noticeable chunk of the population that is always blurry on every single camera across the city is sure to catch the authorities attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:45:23-08:00","id":790462,"title":"","content":"They don't appear blurry as of second edition.<br /> <br /> But it seems like Woland knows what he wants. You'd just have certain agencies, like law enforcement and government or security to have a higher threshold for technology and that might extend to the public marketplace. They might look through the inspirations they want and see what is capable. Simply making the Computers skill more worthwhile, if there was some sort of world-encompassing Matrix, would go a longer way to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-21-2015, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:52:15-08:00","id":790465,"title":"","content":"For Vampire: The Masquerade there was a series of articles in the White Wolf Magazine called &quot;A future world of darkness&quot;. All the magazines containing the articles should be available via DriveThru. <br /> <br /> My suggestion would be:<br /> - Take a look at some Cyperpunk game and decide how to simulate the enhancement aspects (probably equipment bonues ramped up to 3-5 dice).<br /> - Surveillance technology is either purely narratively or you use a system for breaking the Masquerade and ramp it up. I think there is a dice system in one of the SAS adventures. Instead of starting at one dice start at three for example to increase the likelihood of a Masquerade breach occuring when the players do something stupid.<br /> - Describe an environment where information technology is more prevalent. Take cues from Fringe's Red Universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T03:50:52-08:00","id":790789,"title":"","content":"I'd tap into Shadowrun, personally. The suggested technology is advanced enough for your game needs, and should give you some ideas on how to run some aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}